\section*{Ex 2.47 } 
For $A = A^\dagger$ and $B = B^\dagger$, show that $i[A,B]$ is Hermitian.  
$$
(i [A,B])^\dagger = i^\dagger [A,B]^\dagger = -i [B^\dagger, A^\dagger] = -i [B,A] = i [A,B].
$$  
Thus, $i[A,B]$ is Hermitian.


